            <ArticleTitle>A rare condition of Hand-Schüller-Christian disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>759-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present the clinical case of a 61-year-old patient with Hand-Schüller-Christian disease associated with multisystemic involvement. The onset of such puzzling symptoms and the extremely rarity of this disease in a patient of such advanced age resulted in a delayed diagnosis and subsequently delayed treatment of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
